    "group": "pi",
    "order": 0,
    "bio": "Marcelo Dietrich is Professor of Comparative Medicine and of Neuroscience at Yale School of Medicine and the Robert T. McCloskey Scholar. Trained as a physician and biochemist, he leads the Laboratory of Physiology of Behavior, which studies how the brain and body communicate to shape behavior and health across the lifespan — from the neural circuits that build social behavior in early life, to body–brain and immune signaling, to the comparative biology of the nine-banded armadillo. He is also a member of Yale’s Wu Tsai Institute, contributing to its Center for Neurocognition & Behavior and Center for Neurodevelopment & Plasticity.",
